===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʷem-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|comen}}, {{m|enm|cumen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cuman}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*kweman}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*kwemaną|t=to come}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*gʷémt||to step}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*gʷem-|t=to step}}.

{{rel-top|cognates}}
Cognate from Proto-Germanic with {{cog|sco|cum||to come}}, {{cog|stq|kuume||to come}}, {{cog|fy|komme||to come}}, {{cog|nds|kamen||to come}}, {{cog|nl|komen||to come}}, {{cog|de|kommen||to come}}, {{cog|nb|-}} and {{cog|da|komme||to come}}, {{cog|sv|komma||to come}}, {{cog|nn|-}} and {{cog|is|koma||to come}}.

Cognate from PIE via Latin {{m|la|veniō||come, arrive}} with many Romance language terms (e.g., French {{m|fr|venir}}, Portuguese {{m|pt|vir}}, Spanish {{m|es|venir}}), Lithuanian {{m|lt|gimti||to be born, come into the world, arrive}}, with terms in Iranian languages (e.g. {{cog|ae|𐬘𐬀𐬨𐬀𐬌𐬙𐬌|t=to go}}), via Sanskrit {{m|sa|गच्छति||tr=gácchati|to go}} with many Indic language terms (e.g., Hindi {{m|hi|गति}}).

Cognate to {{cog|en|basis}}, from PIE via Ancient Greek.
